00:47:25,583 --> 00:47:26,708
Hey, wait a minute.

974
00:47:31,041 --> 00:47:34,125
Look, tell me how I can persuade you
to stay out of our way this weekend.

975
00:47:35,125 --> 00:47:37,041
Hm… Hmm…

976
00:47:39,333 --> 00:47:40,833
How about cryotherapy?

977
00:47:41,541 --> 00:47:45,083
Whoever can bear
-60 degrees longest… wins.

978
00:47:48,041 --> 00:47:49,208
If I win, we have a deal?

979
00:47:49,791 --> 00:47:50,625
Yeah.

980
00:47:51,791 --> 00:47:54,125
Well, then I'll leave right now.
I'll see you there.

981
00:47:59,291 --> 00:48:00,208
I'm ready…

982
00:48:00,916 --> 00:48:02,083
[laughs]

983
00:48:04,708 --> 00:48:07,625
Wait a minute, Björn.
Why don't we go really extreme, huh?

984
00:48:07,708 --> 00:48:10,791
Let's crank it up to -70. How about that?

985
00:48:10,875 --> 00:48:12,541
-But why don't we--
-Mm?

986
00:48:13,541 --> 00:48:15,583
Come on, let's hit the maximum.

987
00:48:15,666 --> 00:48:16,583
Hm?

988
00:48:19,916 --> 00:48:22,458
Björn? The maximum.

989
00:48:23,541 --> 00:48:24,833
Whatever you want.

990
00:48:26,041 --> 00:48:27,458
Minus 110.

991
00:48:28,916 --> 00:48:30,916
[suspenseful music playing]

992
00:48:58,125 --> 00:48:58,958
Three minutes.

993
00:49:09,708 --> 00:49:10,625
Five minutes.

994
00:49:20,166 --> 00:49:21,041
Ten minutes.

995
00:49:26,208 --> 00:49:29,458
[Olli shuddering]

996
00:49:29,541 --> 00:49:30,875
Just breathe, yeah that's good.

997
00:49:30,958 --> 00:49:33,333
Whoa! That was really good.

998
00:49:33,416 --> 00:49:36,000
Let's do that more often.
Go ahead, give it to him.

999
00:49:36,083 --> 00:49:38,458
All right. That's good.

1000
00:49:40,708 --> 00:49:44,625
W-what the… h- how did she… do that?

1001
00:49:47,208 --> 00:49:49,583
Well, some women have
heightened blood circulation.

1002
00:49:49,666 --> 00:49:51,291
Something about their hormones.

1003
00:49:53,500 --> 00:49:54,708
So what about our deal?

1004
00:49:55,333 --> 00:49:56,916
It stands.

1005
00:50:03,250 --> 00:50:04,125
Thanks.

1006
00:50:05,541 --> 00:50:07,208
Little expensive for cold therapy.

1007
00:50:07,291 --> 00:50:08,666
Worth every cent.

1008
00:50:12,625 --> 00:50:16,333
Looks like we have everything.
Okay great. Time to hit the road.

1009
00:50:34,291 --> 00:50:35,208
[Schmitti, quiet] <i>Olli!</i>

1010
00:50:35,291 --> 00:50:37,625
Schmitti, what's happening?
Wanna grab a drink?

1011
00:50:37,708 --> 00:50:39,958
[Schmitti] <i>I can't.</i>
<i>I'm under house arrest.</i>

1012
00:50:40,041 --> 00:50:41,250
You got put on house arrest?

1013
00:50:41,333 --> 00:50:44,250
[Schmitti] <i>Yeah, sorry, I can't talk</i>
<i>too loud. Antje is listening right now.</i>

1014
00:50:44,333 --> 00:50:46,375
C'mon, would you speak up?
I can barely hear you, man.

1015
00:50:46,458 --> 00:50:48,708
[Schmitti] <i>No, I can't, okay?</i>
<i>Antje is listening.</i>

1016
00:50:48,791 --> 00:50:51,416
Hey, man, Schmitti,
are you in prison? Jesus!

1017
00:50:51,500 --> 00:50:53,666
I mean, it's worse. Prisoners go outdoors.

1018
00:50:53,750 --> 00:50:57,333
-[Schmitti] <i>My hands are tied, man.</i>
-Yeah. Yeah, understood. Forget it.

1019
00:50:59,583 --> 00:51:00,625
[sighs]

1020
00:51:09,208 --> 00:51:10,833
Come on, let's hit the maximum.

1021
00:51:14,375 --> 00:51:16,666
Okay, everyone, how we feeling today!?

1022
00:51:16,750 --> 00:51:17,916
[all cheer]

1023
00:51:18,000 --> 00:51:21,416
Yeah, super!
All right, guys, let's clap it out!

1024
00:51:23,458 --> 00:51:28,625
{\an8}Good! Okay! Good! Okay, nice! Super!
Keep moving those arms, ladies!

1025
00:51:30,416 --> 00:51:31,875
[Olli, muffled] I knew it. Screw you!

1026
00:51:31,958 --> 00:51:33,333
Yeah! And four!

1027
00:51:35,000 --> 00:51:37,000
[soft music playing]

1028
00:51:39,916 --> 00:51:40,958
[seagull calling]

1029
00:51:41,791 --> 00:51:43,166
[electronic beep and whir]

1030
00:51:46,125 --> 00:51:47,333
[screams]

1031
00:51:47,416 --> 00:51:50,041
-[TV on in background]
-[Olli chuckles]

1032
00:51:50,708 --> 00:51:53,208
Olli? What's going on?

1033
00:51:54,125 --> 00:51:54,958
Ask Rebecca.

1034
00:51:55,041 --> 00:51:56,250
We had a deal, you moron.

1035
00:51:56,333 --> 00:51:57,458
The game was rigged!

1036
00:51:58,583 --> 00:52:00,666
Can someone please tell me
what's going on?

1037
00:52:01,208 --> 00:52:03,916
Olli agreed that I could
take you on this trip this weekend.

1038
00:52:04,000 --> 00:52:07,291
But to convince him, I had to last
longer in the cryo thing at -110.

1039
00:52:07,375 --> 00:52:10,500
Gimme a break!
Björn put it at -5 degrees for you,

1040
00:52:10,583 --> 00:52:11,791
that backstabbing meathead.

1041
00:52:11,875 --> 00:52:12,833
The deal's off!

1042
00:52:14,708 --> 00:52:17,291
Listen, I had planned for us
to do some SCUBA stuff this weekend,

1043
00:52:17,375 --> 00:52:20,458
but the doctor over here
made it clear she wouldn't have it.

1044
00:52:20,541 --> 00:52:22,833
So you were… competing over me?

1045
00:52:22,916 --> 00:52:24,333
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

1046
00:52:27,500 --> 00:52:29,250
Uh, wait a minute,
how did you get in here?

1047
00:52:29,333 --> 00:52:30,250
Bribed the maid.

1048
00:52:32,625 --> 00:52:34,125
I can be charming, okay?

1049
00:52:34,750 --> 00:52:37,500
You're an idiot.
And you're covering all this.

1050
00:52:39,708 --> 00:52:41,708
-[slurping]
-Didn't we schedule a body wrap?

1051
00:52:41,791 --> 00:52:43,291
Maybe you should do it with Olli.

1052
00:52:56,916 --> 00:53:00,166
I've been thinking about our trip
a lot more lately, man.

1053
00:53:00,250 --> 00:53:01,666
Good, glad to hear it.

1054
00:53:01,750 --> 00:53:03,500
Gotta get those flights booked.

1055
00:53:03,583 --> 00:53:06,125
Oh, I found
some really cheap ones to Bangkok.

1056
00:53:07,958 --> 00:53:08,958
That's not what I meant.

1057
00:53:13,625 --> 00:53:16,125
I've been talking about it
with Becky for a while now.

1058
00:53:16,208 --> 00:53:17,208
And she won't let you go.

1059
00:53:17,291 --> 00:53:18,541
Not at all!

1060
00:53:18,625 --> 00:53:21,708
She even said I should go for it
if it's my dream, I'm not kidding.

1061
00:53:21,791 --> 00:53:24,375
She's just not sure
if it'd be good for our relationship

1062
00:53:24,458 --> 00:53:26,166
for me to be gone that long, you know?

1063
00:53:26,250 --> 00:53:30,083
Goddammit! Of course!
You're gonna bail because of her.

1064
00:53:31,500 --> 00:53:33,666
How 'bout we compress the trip
down to four weeks?

1065
00:53:33,750 --> 00:53:34,750
Ugh!

1066
00:53:35,458 --> 00:53:36,666
Are you okay?

1067
00:53:36,750 --> 00:53:38,125
[Olli yells]

1068
00:53:39,916 --> 00:53:41,958
It's not a Disney World trip.

1069
00:53:42,041 --> 00:53:43,875
This could really change our lives, man.

1070
00:53:44,583 --> 00:53:45,458
I know that.

1071
00:53:45,541 --> 00:53:47,291
You wanna miss out on this opportunity?

1072
00:53:47,375 --> 00:53:50,166
You wanna keep working
that stupid job all day?

1073
00:53:50,250 --> 00:53:52,375
To buy some townhouse in suburbia
like Schmitti?

1074
00:53:52,458 --> 00:53:54,125
Dude, I don't know yet.

1075
00:53:55,833 --> 00:53:58,250
But I actually like that job, Olli, okay?

1076
00:54:01,125 --> 00:54:02,458
I'm sorry, Olli.

1077
00:54:03,291 --> 00:54:05,291
[melancholy music playing]

1078
00:54:09,291 --> 00:54:11,500
[aggressive rock music playing]

1079
00:54:11,583 --> 00:54:12,541
[phone pings]

1080
00:54:16,666 --> 00:54:19,583
[Schmitti] <i>Hi, Olli. You said you wanted</i>
<i>to grab a beer sometime, right?</i>

1081
00:54:19,666 --> 00:54:23,166
<i>Antje is going to the movies tonight,</i>
<i>so I'll be free from eight to ten.</i>

1082
00:54:23,250 --> 00:54:24,541
<i>Let me know if that works, okay?</i>

1083
00:54:26,791 --> 00:54:28,791
[engine accelerating]

1084
00:54:38,333 --> 00:54:40,208
-Olli!
-Explain how it's possible

1085
00:54:40,291 --> 00:54:42,375
-your girlfriends are brainwashing you!
-Calm down.

1086
00:54:42,458 --> 00:54:44,000
What's the matter with you, Olli?

1087
00:54:44,083 --> 00:54:45,875
Matze canceled our trip around the world.

1088
00:54:47,791 --> 00:54:50,083
[laughs] Hang on, you thought
you were still gonna do that?

1089
00:54:50,166 --> 00:54:51,583
Uh, yeah.

1090
00:54:52,375 --> 00:54:55,291
Olli, Matze has a woman in his life now.

1091
00:54:55,375 --> 00:54:58,958
I mean, he'd be stupid not to choose his
relationship over a year-long world tour.

1092
00:54:59,541 --> 00:55:00,541
That's your opinion.

1093
00:55:00,625 --> 00:55:03,166
The opinion of a guy
who calls his wife a cow's ass.

1094
00:55:03,250 --> 00:55:04,583
I was drunk.

1095
00:55:04,666 --> 00:55:06,375
It could be worse with Antje.

1096
00:55:07,250 --> 00:55:09,000
When we're alone, she's kinda nice.

1097
00:55:09,500 --> 00:55:12,541
"Kinda nice"?
Was that what you always hoped for?

1098
00:55:12,625 --> 00:55:15,916
Got someone better, hm?
It's not like women are lining up for me.

1099
00:55:16,000 --> 00:55:19,583
Besides, if Antje hadn't
pushed me so hard, I would never have…

1100
00:55:19,666 --> 00:55:21,708
made it to department supervisor.

1101
00:55:21,791 --> 00:55:25,458
And I wouldn't have wound up with…
a fancy office and view of the cathedral.

1102
00:55:28,708 --> 00:55:31,416
Seriously, man,
I'm really glad she's my wife.

1103
00:55:34,750 --> 00:55:37,000
So what about tonight?
Are we going out for a beer, then?

1104
00:55:37,083 --> 00:55:40,375
Nah, forget it. Probably better
to stay in and iron Antje's panties.

1105
00:55:40,458 --> 00:55:41,625
[gasps]

1106
00:55:41,708 --> 00:55:43,708
[aggressive rock music playing]

1107
00:55:45,250 --> 00:55:48,666
Olli! You can't be selfish in life!
Compromise is paramount.

1108
00:55:59,708 --> 00:56:00,833
What are you doing?

1109
00:56:01,416 --> 00:56:02,458
Leaving.

1110
00:56:11,500 --> 00:56:12,416
[Matze] Okay, why?

1111
00:56:13,416 --> 00:56:15,416
Because I'm done
getting screwed over here.

1112
00:56:15,500 --> 00:56:17,958
You're not even looking
for a new place for her, dude.

1113
00:56:18,041 --> 00:56:19,583
That's not true, man.

1114
00:56:19,666 --> 00:56:21,666
I showed Becky two places,
and neither felt right.

1115
00:56:21,750 --> 00:56:26,750
Two? Well! Man, that's tough.
You really want her outta here, don't you?

1116
00:56:29,041 --> 00:56:32,333
You're right, I… let it slide for a while.

1117
00:56:32,416 --> 00:56:35,458
I thought the three of us would find
common ground and start getting along.

1118
00:56:37,541 --> 00:56:38,875
C'mon, you sure you wanna do this?

1119
00:56:40,541 --> 00:56:41,666
Yeah.

1120
00:56:45,083 --> 00:56:46,791
[melancholy music playing]

1121
00:56:46,875 --> 00:56:47,833
Okay.

1122
00:57:02,333 --> 00:57:03,166
Do you need help?

1123
00:57:04,583 --> 00:57:05,666
Not going fast enough?

1124
00:57:07,958 --> 00:57:09,458
Don't be so angry at Matze, okay?

1125
00:57:10,458 --> 00:57:13,625
It's understandable that he doesn't
want us to be apart for a full year.

1126
00:57:14,750 --> 00:57:16,833
Yeah, because it was
all his decision, right?

1127
00:57:16,916 --> 00:57:19,000
-Of course it was.
-[Olli laughs]

1128
00:57:20,125 --> 00:57:21,500
Okay, whatever, doctor.

1129
00:57:22,458 --> 00:57:24,833
Do you really think I'm as dumb as I look?

1130
00:57:24,916 --> 00:57:26,916
I know why you wanted to spend
a long weekend alone

1131
00:57:27,000 --> 00:57:28,125
with my best friend, alright?

1132
00:57:28,791 --> 00:57:32,083
And I also know that that whole
plumbing thing was a total excuse.

1133
00:57:33,583 --> 00:57:35,541
And the more I think about the situation,

1134
00:57:35,625 --> 00:57:38,750
I'd be a fool to just sit back
and let you win, so, uh…

1135
00:57:41,458 --> 00:57:45,166
Hello? Excuse me? Oh, I see.
That's too bad. Goodbye.

1136
00:57:47,791 --> 00:57:49,250
Bad luck, I guess.

1137
00:57:49,791 --> 00:57:53,208
My building manager told me
the unit I wanted isn't available anymore.

1138
00:57:53,291 --> 00:57:54,500
Oh, well.

1139
00:57:54,583 --> 00:57:55,541
I'll be staying.

1140
00:58:06,708 --> 00:58:09,625
So, your roommate just had
a chat with his right hand.

1141
00:58:09,708 --> 00:58:10,958
He's not planning on moving out.

1142
00:58:11,041 --> 00:58:13,750
Yeah, sorry, it didn't work out after all.

1143
00:58:13,833 --> 00:58:16,291
But it's not so bad.
We get to live together. Eh?

1144
00:58:16,375 --> 00:58:17,750
It's worked out well so far.

1145
00:58:17,833 --> 00:58:20,500
Worked out well? Are you serious?

1146
00:58:20,583 --> 00:58:21,833
Are you guys outta your mind?

1147
00:58:21,916 --> 00:58:24,041
For weeks, you've been acting like kids.

1148
00:58:24,125 --> 00:58:26,000
Either figure it out and grow up

1149
00:58:26,083 --> 00:58:27,833
or just ignore each other
and just move on.

1150
00:58:27,916 --> 00:58:29,166
Watch out, my friend.

1151
00:58:30,291 --> 00:58:31,416
[laughs]

1152
00:58:31,500 --> 00:58:33,666
'Watch out'? Becky can be so domineering.

1153
00:58:33,750 --> 00:58:36,458
Telling me where to look. Women.

1154
00:58:37,041 --> 00:58:39,500
["The Only One I Know"
by The Charlatans playing]

1155
00:58:50,541 --> 00:58:53,833
<i>♪ The only one I know ♪</i>

1156
00:58:54,375 --> 00:58:57,958
<i>♪ Has come to take me away ♪</i>

1157
00:58:58,458 --> 00:59:01,791
<i>♪ The only one I know ♪</i>

1158
00:59:02,375 --> 00:59:05,750
<i>♪ Is mine when she stitches me ♪</i>

1159
00:59:10,375 --> 00:59:13,583
<i>♪ The only one I see ♪</i>

1160
00:59:14,208 --> 00:59:15,833
<i>♪ Has found an aching in me ♪</i>

1161
00:59:15,916 --> 00:59:17,083
[screams]

1162
00:59:18,291 --> 00:59:19,958
<i>♪ The only one I see ♪</i>

1163
00:59:20,041 --> 00:59:20,916
[Olli screaming]

1164
00:59:22,000 --> 00:59:25,166
<i>♪ Has turned her tongue into me ♪</i>

1165
00:59:27,000 --> 00:59:28,375
Beautiful teeth.

1166
00:59:29,625 --> 00:59:36,291
<i>♪ Everyone has been burned before ♪</i>

1167
00:59:39,750 --> 00:59:43,083
CREATE AD FOR SALE

1168
00:59:49,000 --> 00:59:49,833
[machine] <i>Jackpot!</i>

1169
00:59:49,916 --> 00:59:50,750
[doorbell ringing]

1170
00:59:50,833 --> 00:59:52,375
<i>♪ The only one I know ♪</i>

1171
00:59:52,458 --> 00:59:53,958
Hello. For the pinball machine?

1172
00:59:55,000 --> 00:59:55,875
What now?

1173
00:59:55,958 --> 00:59:58,291
Look, I bought it for one euro.
Great deal.

1174
00:59:58,375 --> 00:59:59,958
<i>♪ The only one I know ♪</i>

1175
01:00:00,041 --> 01:00:01,916
Oh, whatever, man.

1176
01:00:02,000 --> 01:00:04,750
Hey! Open the door!
Bring it out here right now!

1177
01:00:04,833 --> 01:00:06,583
Ow! No! Hey! Hey!

1178
01:00:06,666 --> 01:00:08,375
Open the door! What's going on?

1179
01:00:09,708 --> 01:00:13,000
<i>♪ The only one I see ♪</i>

1180
01:00:13,583 --> 01:00:17,083
<i>♪ Is mine when she walks down the street ♪</i>

1181
01:00:17,708 --> 01:00:21,500
<i>♪ The only one I see ♪</i>

1182
01:00:21,583 --> 01:00:25,000
<i>♪ Has carved her way into me ♪</i>

1183
01:00:29,458 --> 01:00:34,916
<i>♪ Everyone has been burned before ♪</i>

1184
01:00:35,000 --> 01:00:36,458
Ah! Ah!

1185
01:00:37,000 --> 01:00:37,833
Fuck.

1186
01:00:38,541 --> 01:00:39,416
[groans]

1187
01:00:43,541 --> 01:00:44,375
Whoa!

1188
01:00:44,875 --> 01:00:47,375
<i>♪ Everyone ♪</i>

1189
01:00:47,458 --> 01:00:48,791
Oh my God, oh my God.

1190
01:00:48,875 --> 01:00:52,458
<i>♪ …burned before ♪</i>

1191
01:00:54,583 --> 01:00:56,875
Agh! Agh!

1192
01:00:56,958 --> 01:00:58,041
BEST BEFORE AUGUST 2008

1193
01:00:58,125 --> 01:00:59,916
Dammit. Ugh!

1194
01:01:00,000 --> 01:01:01,125
Ah!

1195
01:01:01,208 --> 01:01:03,125
-[popping]
-Ah! Ah!

1196
01:01:28,125 --> 01:01:28,958
What happened?

1197
01:01:29,916 --> 01:01:31,750
[melancholy music playing]

1198
01:01:31,833 --> 01:01:34,000
Uh, Olli had a sandwich issue.

1199
01:01:34,541 --> 01:01:36,166
[Olli] The sandwich press caught on fire.

1200
01:01:36,250 --> 01:01:38,125
I have no idea what happened, sorry.

1201
01:01:58,125 --> 01:02:00,791
Uh, maybe it was, um, a sign

1202
01:02:02,000 --> 01:02:04,416
that you and I should
think about finding a new place.

1203
01:02:06,500 --> 01:02:08,875
So, I have this patient,
she's a really sweet old lady,

1204
01:02:08,958 --> 01:02:10,958
and she's got this apartment.

1205
01:02:11,041 --> 01:02:12,541
She wants to rent it out.

1206
01:02:13,541 --> 01:02:15,333
She told me we'd be perfect.

1207
01:02:19,041 --> 01:02:22,000
So, what's she talking you into
this time, huh?

1208
01:02:24,666 --> 01:02:28,458
[Rebecca, muffled] Listen, I'm sorry about
what happened. I… didn't want any of this.

1209
01:02:28,541 --> 01:02:31,666
[Matze, muffled] Don't worry about it.
I'm just happy neither of you got hurt.

1210
01:02:31,750 --> 01:02:35,583
As for the place, well, to be honest,
my pride as a realtor is a little damaged

1211
01:02:35,666 --> 01:02:39,500
since you found it first…
but this unit looks awesome, Becky.

1212
01:02:39,583 --> 01:02:40,458
Yeah, I know!

1213
01:02:40,541 --> 01:02:42,166
I think we should just go for it.

1214
01:02:47,750 --> 01:02:51,041
Uh… There's one tiny little stipulation.

1215
01:02:52,333 --> 01:02:54,666
Just meet her once,
and she'll be glad to give her approval.

1216
01:02:55,250 --> 01:02:56,708
Okay. When and where?

1217
01:02:56,791 --> 01:02:59,583
Day after tomorrow.
Just meet her in the unit, that's all.

1218
01:02:59,666 --> 01:03:01,291
Day after tomorrow is your conference.

1219
01:03:01,916 --> 01:03:04,125
Uh, yeah, but it'll be fine.
I don't need to be there.

1220
01:03:04,208 --> 01:03:08,000
Just stop by, say a quick hello, and…
and then we have the apartment.

1221
01:03:09,875 --> 01:03:13,416
[rock music playing]

1222
01:03:13,500 --> 01:03:15,333
[Matze] Sounds good, Miss Akçay.
See you later.

1223
01:03:17,041 --> 01:03:21,541
Hey, uh, I've been thinking about your
decision not to go on our trip anymore,

1224
01:03:21,625 --> 01:03:24,750
and well, um…
Well, I'm good with it. Yeah.

1225
01:03:26,791 --> 01:03:27,750
Nice of you to say.

1226
01:03:27,833 --> 01:03:28,791
Mm.

1227
01:03:28,875 --> 01:03:31,041
Man, you know,
I just wish I could do both.

1228
01:03:31,916 --> 01:03:35,208
Travel the globe with you
and get to be with Becky at the same time.

1229
01:03:36,500 --> 01:03:41,916
What if instead of a big world tour,
we uh… just changed it to a small one?

1230
01:03:43,166 --> 01:03:46,125
Here in the city.
A single night to make it happen.

1231
01:03:47,750 --> 01:03:49,166
What are you saying?

1232
01:03:49,250 --> 01:03:50,333
I'll surprise you.

1233
01:03:51,166 --> 01:03:54,541
I'll say this much,
we're starting in Bangkok.

1234
01:03:55,416 --> 01:03:56,458
Okay?

1235
01:03:57,458 --> 01:03:58,291
Great, yep.

1236
01:04:02,208 --> 01:04:03,833
CONFIRMATION
THANK YOU FOR PURCHASING TICKETS

1237
01:04:03,916 --> 01:04:05,583
-Hi, Becky.
-[Rebecca] <i>Hey, are you busy?</i>

1238
01:04:05,666 --> 01:04:07,125
No, all good.

1239
01:04:07,208 --> 01:04:10,458
Olli just pitched
a scaled-down version of our trip.

1240
01:04:10,541 --> 01:04:11,625
I wouldn't trust that.

1241
01:04:11,708 --> 01:04:14,458
It's all right.
He's trying to be nice, that's all.

1242
01:04:15,375 --> 01:04:17,208
Just don't forget,
you're meeting her tomorrow.

1243
01:04:17,291 --> 01:04:18,708
Don't worry, I'll remember.

1244
01:04:20,041 --> 01:04:22,458
I can't bail on this idea too, though.

1245
01:04:22,541 --> 01:04:24,000
He's already done all the legwork.

1246
01:04:28,625 --> 01:04:30,000
No, it's just tonight.

1247
01:04:31,458 --> 01:04:32,833
It's not gonna take long.

1248
01:04:36,500 --> 01:04:39,375
[Olli] Woohoo! This is a Mekong Sour.

1249
01:04:40,291 --> 01:04:41,250
[clinking]

1250
01:04:44,458 --> 01:04:45,291
Mm.

1251
01:04:45,958 --> 01:04:49,208
Mm. Fried grasshoppers are
a popular snack in Thailand.

1252
01:04:49,833 --> 01:04:51,458
Extremely protein-rich as well.

1253
01:04:53,750 --> 01:04:56,750
Hey, smile.
The Thai are very sensitive to manners.

1254
01:05:00,041 --> 01:05:01,000
Bottoms up.

1255
01:05:02,208 --> 01:05:03,083
Hm?

1256
01:05:03,166 --> 01:05:04,666
Mm. Mm.

1257
01:05:06,000 --> 01:05:07,416
We're leaving Thailand for now…

1258
01:05:07,500 --> 01:05:10,625
-Huh?
-…and catching a flight to Siberia.

1259
01:05:14,916 --> 01:05:16,916
[wind whistling]

1260
01:05:23,083 --> 01:05:24,041
-Hey, uh…
-Uh…

1261
01:05:24,125 --> 01:05:25,083
Ah!

1262
01:05:25,166 --> 01:05:27,083
-Whoa. Oh, Jesus.
-Ugh…

1263
01:05:28,416 --> 01:05:29,791
Ah! Ah!

1264
01:05:30,500 --> 01:05:32,041
[Matze] Let's go back to a warm country.

1265
01:05:32,125 --> 01:05:35,166
[playing "La Bamba"]

1266
01:05:35,250 --> 01:05:37,250
[singing in Spanish]

1267
01:05:45,125 --> 01:05:46,458
[Olli] Hey!

1268
01:05:49,333 --> 01:05:52,416
In the real Acapulco,
we'd be on the beach now.

1269
01:06:05,541 --> 01:06:08,333
It would be so great
to go on a real journey around the world.

1270
01:06:09,250 --> 01:06:11,958
I'm glad you said that, dude.
Because actually…

1271
01:06:12,041 --> 01:06:16,083
[phone buzzing]

1272
01:06:18,250 --> 01:06:19,083
Hi, honey.

1273
01:06:19,166 --> 01:06:20,916
[Rebecca] <i>Hey. Everything okay?</i>

1274
01:06:21,000 --> 01:06:24,375
[Matze] All good. Yeah, uh…
we're in Marrakesh right now.

1275
01:06:24,458 --> 01:06:25,875
[Rebecca] <i>How late you gonna be out?</i>

1276
01:06:25,958 --> 01:06:28,333
Not much longer. Don't worry.

1277
01:06:28,875 --> 01:06:31,041
Don't forget the documents tomorrow, okay?

1278
01:06:31,125 --> 01:06:32,250
I won't forget.

1279
01:06:33,333 --> 01:06:34,666
I'll take care of it all.

1280
01:06:34,750 --> 01:06:35,625
[Rebecca] <i>Good.</i>

1281
01:06:38,083 --> 01:06:40,500
Sorry, I have to head in.
I'll text you later, okay?

1282
01:06:40,583 --> 01:06:41,458
All right, honey.

1283
01:06:42,125 --> 01:06:44,041
Hey. I love you.

1284
01:06:44,666 --> 01:06:45,666
I love you too.

1285
01:06:47,875 --> 01:06:49,250
I love you too.

1286
01:06:51,750 --> 01:06:53,125
Just one more, okay?

1287
01:06:53,208 --> 01:06:54,166
Yeah.

1288
01:06:58,291 --> 01:07:01,583
[dramatic ambient music playing]

1289
01:07:03,000 --> 01:07:05,000
[eagle screeching]

1290
01:07:05,750 --> 01:07:07,125
[Matze] Where are we now?

1291
01:07:07,208 --> 01:07:09,166
-Mongolia.
-[camel grunting]

1292
01:07:09,250 --> 01:07:11,250
The middle of the Gobi.

1293
01:07:12,208 --> 01:07:14,041
The desert Genghis Khan crossed.

1294
01:07:14,125 --> 01:07:15,000
[Matze] Cool.

1295
01:07:15,083 --> 01:07:16,375
-[Ollie laughing]
-[camel grunts]

1296
01:07:16,458 --> 01:07:17,625
[phone buzzes]

1297
01:07:21,041 --> 01:07:22,833
[Rebecca] <i>Hey, we're done for the night.</i>

1298
01:07:22,916 --> 01:07:25,500
<i>Pretty beat, so I'm going to bed.</i>
<i>Where are you right now?</i>

1299
01:07:28,583 --> 01:07:34,791
{\an8}STILL IN MONGOLIA
I'LL CALL YOU IN THE MORNING

1300
01:07:39,333 --> 01:07:41,875
{\an8}STILL IN MONGOLIA
I'LL CALL YOU IN THE MORNING

1301
01:07:43,625 --> 01:07:47,791
Welcome to Africa.
You get the snacks, I'll get the drinks.

1302
01:07:48,333 --> 01:07:50,916
["Bohemian Like You"
by The Dandy Warhols playing]

1303
01:07:58,166 --> 01:08:00,000
<i>♪ You've got a great car ♪</i>

1304
01:08:00,833 --> 01:08:02,833
<i>♪ Yeah, what's wrong with it today? ♪</i>

1305
01:08:02,916 --> 01:08:04,666
Healthy and delicious!

1306
01:08:05,250 --> 01:08:07,166
Dude, I want junk food, okay?

1307
01:08:07,250 --> 01:08:10,750
[woman laughing] Beautiful.
Seriously, I'm so excited.

1308
01:08:10,833 --> 01:08:14,250
[conversing indistinctly]

1309
01:08:14,791 --> 01:08:18,541
I'm not kidding, I'm gonna tell everyone
I know. Get ready for a spike in business.

1310
01:08:20,083 --> 01:08:22,083
<i>♪ So what do you do? ♪</i>

1311
01:08:24,125 --> 01:08:25,208
[Matze] Where to now?

1312
01:08:26,083 --> 01:08:27,541
The coast of Argentina.

1313
01:08:28,041 --> 01:08:30,083
But first we better get a little snack.

1314
01:08:30,166 --> 01:08:33,458
<i>♪…on vegan food</i>
<i>Well, come over to my work ♪</i>

1315
01:08:33,541 --> 01:08:37,083
<i>♪ I'll have them cook you something</i>
<i>That you'll really love ♪</i>

1316
01:08:37,166 --> 01:08:40,625
<i>♪ 'Cause I like you</i>
<i>Yeah, I like you ♪</i>

1317
01:08:40,708 --> 01:08:44,500
<i>♪ And I'm feeling so bohemian like you ♪</i>

1318
01:08:44,583 --> 01:08:48,041
<i>♪ Yeah, I like you</i>
<i>Yeah, I like you ♪</i>

1319
01:08:48,125 --> 01:08:50,791
<i>♪ And I feel</i>
<i>Whoa, whoo! ♪</i>

1320
01:09:05,333 --> 01:09:07,041
We're in Argentina!

1321
01:09:07,583 --> 01:09:09,833
[both] Whoo!

1322
01:09:25,416 --> 01:09:26,916
[song ends]

1323
01:09:27,000 --> 01:09:29,000
[caws]

1324
01:09:49,625 --> 01:09:50,666
Becky?

1325
01:09:51,791 --> 01:09:53,208
Welcome to Argentina.

1326
01:09:53,291 --> 01:09:54,500
Did you forget?

1327
01:09:54,583 --> 01:09:56,875
-You have location sharing turned on!
-[groans]

1328
01:09:56,958 --> 01:10:00,500
The apartment viewing was an hour ago.
And you look like a homeless guy!

1329
01:10:00,583 --> 01:10:04,166
[man] Hey, sweet cheeks!
Would you keep your voice down?

1330
01:10:04,250 --> 01:10:06,083
For God's sake, we're trying to sleep!

1331
01:10:06,166 --> 01:10:07,041
[Becky] I get it now.

1332
01:10:07,708 --> 01:10:10,791
You were never really
that interested in being with me.

1333
01:10:11,750 --> 01:10:12,583
My bad.

1334
01:10:13,583 --> 01:10:17,000
Wait! Becky… Becky. Becky.

1335
01:10:18,000 --> 01:10:20,791
It was a m…mistake.

1336
01:10:20,875 --> 01:10:22,208
I'm s-s-sorry.

1337
01:10:27,583 --> 01:10:28,625
[Olli laughing]

1338
01:10:28,708 --> 01:10:30,958
Dude, your hair. What the hell happened?

1339
01:10:32,583 --> 01:10:34,125
[Rebecca] Gotta be kidding.

1340
01:10:34,208 --> 01:10:36,625
Shit, no… Becky.

1341
01:10:38,416 --> 01:10:39,333
Becky.

1342
01:10:40,750 --> 01:10:41,708
Shit!

1343
01:10:50,375 --> 01:10:52,500
[sing-song] Fresh rolls!

1344
01:10:54,083 --> 01:10:55,166
[sighs]

1345
01:10:58,958 --> 01:10:59,791
What's going on?

1346
01:11:03,750 --> 01:11:04,958
She broke it off with me.

1347
01:11:07,208 --> 01:11:08,041
Really?

1348
01:11:19,833 --> 01:11:21,083
Uh…

1349
01:11:21,166 --> 01:11:23,541
"Unfortunately,
I've come to the realization

1350
01:11:23,625 --> 01:11:25,000
that you'll never grow up."

1351
01:11:25,083 --> 01:11:30,250
I want a man, not some overgrown,
uh, chick… child."

1352
01:11:30,333 --> 01:11:31,958
Her handwriting is a disaster.

1353
01:11:32,041 --> 01:11:33,416
"I tried everything with you,

1354
01:11:33,500 --> 01:11:37,958
but apparently you're only happy
if you have Olli by your side."

1355
01:11:38,041 --> 01:11:39,958
Hm, she nailed that one at least.

1356
01:11:40,041 --> 01:11:42,041
"I hope you have a nice life with him."

1357
01:11:44,375 --> 01:11:45,708
I can't believe this.

1358
01:11:53,000 --> 01:11:53,833
Hm?

1359
01:11:57,375 --> 01:11:59,541
An around-the-world ticket?

1360
01:11:59,625 --> 01:12:01,791
I tapped into
our world tour account, Matze.

1361
01:12:06,958 --> 01:12:08,625
You got these tickets
before she dumped me,

1362
01:12:08,708 --> 01:12:09,750
what's the matter with you?

1363
01:12:13,458 --> 01:12:15,750
Unbelievable. You're not my friend.

1364
01:12:15,833 --> 01:12:17,750
Oh my God, you're an asshole!

1365
01:12:18,333 --> 01:12:19,208
Hey.

1366
01:12:19,833 --> 01:12:26,625
B… b… b… b… b… b… b…

1367
01:12:35,291 --> 01:12:39,333
Becky was the woman I'd been looking for.

1368
01:12:40,708 --> 01:12:42,166
And I was really happy.

1369
01:12:43,875 --> 01:12:46,958
Hey. That… that's temporary--

1370
01:12:53,125 --> 01:12:54,916
Hey. Relax.

1371
01:12:59,500 --> 01:13:01,458
I wanna pull out of our lease.

1372
01:13:02,666 --> 01:13:04,208
Does that mean you're dumping me?

1373
01:13:05,208 --> 01:13:06,500
Will you go, or should I?

1374
01:13:10,583 --> 01:13:11,708
Yeah, I'll leave.

1375
01:13:15,666 --> 01:13:16,791
Well, I'm out of here.

1376
01:13:17,916 --> 01:13:19,916
["I Miss You" by Blink 182 playing]

1377
01:13:34,958 --> 01:13:39,333
<i>♪ Hello there</i>
<i>The angel from my nightmare ♪</i>

1378
01:13:39,416 --> 01:13:42,291
<i>♪ The shadow in the background</i>
<i>Of the morgue ♪</i>

1379
01:13:42,375 --> 01:13:45,375
<i>♪ The unsuspecting victim ♪</i>

1380
01:13:45,458 --> 01:13:47,500
<i>♪ Of darkness in the valley ♪</i>

1381
01:13:47,583 --> 01:13:49,625
<i>-♪ We can live like Jack and Sally ♪</i>
-Answer it.

1382
01:13:49,708 --> 01:13:50,750
<i>♪ If we want ♪</i>

1383
01:13:51,333 --> 01:13:54,000
<i>♪ Where you can always find me ♪</i>

1384
01:13:54,083 --> 01:13:56,875
<i>♪ We'll have Halloween on Christmas ♪</i>

1385
01:13:56,958 --> 01:13:59,500
<i>♪ And in the night</i>
<i>We'll wish this never ends ♪</i>

1386
01:14:00,083 --> 01:14:01,833
<i>♪ We'll wish this never ends ♪</i>

1387
01:14:01,916 --> 01:14:03,416
[sobbing]

1388
01:14:04,291 --> 01:14:06,291
So… right this way.

1389
01:14:06,791 --> 01:14:09,250
As you can see,
you've got a spacious living area

1390
01:14:09,333 --> 01:14:10,583
and a dining room here.

1391
01:14:10,666 --> 01:14:13,416
The real heart of this unit,
though, is this gorgeous new--

1392
01:14:13,500 --> 01:14:14,666
What's that?

1393
01:14:14,750 --> 01:14:16,958
Uh… um…

1394
01:14:17,625 --> 01:14:18,958
We'll be moving that stuff.

1395
01:14:21,166 --> 01:14:22,166
DONE! YOUR AD IS ONLINE.

1396
01:14:22,833 --> 01:14:24,583
<i>♪ Where are you? ♪</i>

1397
01:14:25,083 --> 01:14:27,291
<i>♪ And I'm so sorry ♪</i>

1398
01:14:27,375 --> 01:14:30,333
<i>♪ I cannot sleep, I cannot dream tonight ♪</i>

1399
01:14:30,416 --> 01:14:33,250
<i>♪ I need somebody, and always ♪</i>

1400
01:14:33,333 --> 01:14:35,916
-[dings]
<i>-♪ This sick, strange darkness ♪</i>

1401
01:14:36,000 --> 01:14:38,041
<i>♪ Comes creeping on</i>
<i>So haunting every time ♪</i>

1402
01:14:38,125 --> 01:14:40,041
PIA93 BOUGHT THE "AROUND THE WORLD TICKET"

1403
01:14:40,125 --> 01:14:42,375
<i>♪ And as I stared I counted ♪</i>

1404
01:14:42,458 --> 01:14:44,958
<i>♪ The webs from all the spiders ♪</i>

1405
01:14:45,041 --> 01:14:47,666
<i>♪ Catching things</i>
<i>And eating their insides ♪</i>

1406
01:14:47,750 --> 01:14:50,708
<i>♪ Like indecision to call you ♪</i>

1407
01:14:50,791 --> 01:14:52,833
<i>♪ And hear your voice of treason… ♪</i>

1408
01:14:52,916 --> 01:14:53,750
Hey.

1409
01:14:57,875 --> 01:14:59,250
You owe me 24.90.

1410
01:14:59,333 --> 01:15:01,458
Ha. Why? It wasn't your book.

1411
01:15:02,041 --> 01:15:04,250
Yeah, but now
it can't be sold in the store.

1412
01:15:04,875 --> 01:15:06,000
AUSTRALIA

1413
01:15:06,083 --> 01:15:07,250
Holy shit, you must be Pia.

1414
01:15:09,375 --> 01:15:10,333
Does this look familiar?

1415
01:15:11,375 --> 01:15:13,666
You're Olli?
You put up the post for that ticket?

1416
01:15:14,250 --> 01:15:16,125
Yeah. You wanna travel the world then?

1417
01:15:16,958 --> 01:15:18,666
Well, I'm waiting for that 24.90 first.

1418
01:15:32,125 --> 01:15:34,208
I've been dreaming of doing
a trip around the world.

1419
01:15:34,291 --> 01:15:36,708
I feel like everyone says that,
but no one does it.

1420
01:15:36,791 --> 01:15:40,583
Then I knew as soon as I saw your ad
for the plane ticket… I'm gonna go for it.

1421
01:15:40,666 --> 01:15:42,375
-[laughs] Great.
-And you?

1422
01:15:42,458 --> 01:15:44,833
-Mm.
-Lemme guess, your girlfriend ran away

1423
01:15:44,916 --> 01:15:46,833
and now you have
an extra ticket to get rid of.

1424
01:15:46,916 --> 01:15:48,833
Not a girlfriend… uh, boyfriend.

1425
01:15:48,916 --> 01:15:50,666
Sorry, I assumed you were straight.

1426
01:15:50,750 --> 01:15:54,125
I am… well, for now.
But I'm trying to keep my options open.

1427
01:15:54,208 --> 01:15:56,333
Uh-huh. You must not do well with women.

1428
01:15:56,416 --> 01:15:58,208
[scoffs] What makes you think that?

1429
01:15:58,791 --> 01:15:59,708
Just a guess.

1430
01:16:00,583 --> 01:16:01,958
[laughs] Sorry.

1431
01:16:03,333 --> 01:16:05,708
Why'd your friend back outta the trip?
What happened?

1432
01:16:05,791 --> 01:16:07,333
Um… a woman ruined it.

1433
01:16:07,416 --> 01:16:09,333
[laughs]

1434
01:16:09,416 --> 01:16:11,958
[intriguing music playing]

1435
01:16:12,041 --> 01:16:13,000
Okay, let's hear it.

1436
01:16:15,875 --> 01:16:16,916
Oh, come on.

1437
01:16:17,000 --> 01:16:20,166
We might as well start getting acquainted
with each other now, don't you think?

1438
01:16:20,250 --> 01:16:22,500
We're gonna see each other
on planes all the time.

1439
01:16:24,166 --> 01:16:26,083
You're more of a Peter Pan type, huh?

1440
01:16:26,166 --> 01:16:28,125
You mean the little boy
in the green spandex?

1441
01:16:28,208 --> 01:16:30,041
Mmm. He wants to be a kid forever.

1442
01:16:30,125 --> 01:16:33,916
Yeah, but I'm an adult, and spoiler alert:
it hasn't been fun, it's disappointing.

1443
01:16:34,000 --> 01:16:35,875
Your friend obviously doesn't agree.

1444
01:16:36,875 --> 01:16:38,125
Why is that so hard for you?

1445
01:16:40,833 --> 01:16:42,291
Well, 'cause I'm not gonna…

1446
01:16:42,375 --> 01:16:43,458
[Pia] Oh, come on.

1447
01:16:43,541 --> 01:16:45,666
The fact is, you've kinda

1448
01:16:45,750 --> 01:16:48,250
lost sight of his wants
and your relationship in general.

1449
01:16:48,333 --> 01:16:50,041
Sounds like you've been
thinking about yourself.

1450
01:16:50,125 --> 01:16:52,250
Your friend's evolving, and now,

1451
01:16:52,333 --> 01:16:55,333
he's starting to have other concerns
outside of trip he's taking with you.

1452
01:16:57,333 --> 01:16:58,916
Not the first time I've heard that.

1453
01:16:59,666 --> 01:17:02,791
Mm. Sounds like you two need to make up.

1454
01:17:10,458 --> 01:17:12,000
Well, see you at the airport.

1455
01:17:12,583 --> 01:17:14,083
-Uh-huh.
-Thanks for the coffee.

1456
01:17:15,291 --> 01:17:16,750
Uh, yeah.

1457
01:17:16,833 --> 01:17:17,875
[footsteps receding]

1458
01:17:17,958 --> 01:17:19,583
-[Pia] Bye.
-[woman] See ya.

1459
01:17:19,666 --> 01:17:21,666
["Achterbahn" by Clueso playing]

1460
01:17:25,708 --> 01:17:27,291
They're renovating the building.

1461
01:17:27,375 --> 01:17:29,583
[singer singing in German]

1462
01:17:29,666 --> 01:17:30,541
Can you gimme a sec?

1463
01:17:35,708 --> 01:17:37,583
Hey, do you have…

1464
01:17:38,708 --> 01:17:39,833
I'm just, um…

1465
01:17:42,291 --> 01:17:43,375
Hey.

1466
01:17:47,333 --> 01:17:48,500
Okay. Cool.

1467
01:17:48,583 --> 01:17:52,125
[song continues]

1468
01:17:55,541 --> 01:18:00,583
[indistinct dialog]

1469
01:18:10,583 --> 01:18:14,208
Rebecca? Hey! Hey, wait a sec!

1470
01:18:16,250 --> 01:18:17,291
Rebecca!

1471
01:18:18,625 --> 01:18:21,625
Hey, just one second, okay? Can we talk?

1472
01:18:23,916 --> 01:18:25,833
[screaming]

1473
01:18:28,291 --> 01:18:30,458
[coughing and retching]

1474
01:18:30,541 --> 01:18:33,000
[Olli yelling in pain]

1475
01:18:37,833 --> 01:18:39,833
[song continues]

1476
01:18:45,958 --> 01:18:47,833
Mister… Pan?

1477
01:18:51,166 --> 01:18:52,166
Yeah.

1478
01:18:53,083 --> 01:18:53,916
Please.

1479
01:18:56,125 --> 01:18:56,958
Mm.

1480
01:19:00,833 --> 01:19:02,041
-Take a seat.
-Okay.

1481
01:19:02,916 --> 01:19:04,833
-All right…
-Oh. Uh…

1482
01:19:06,291 --> 01:19:07,458
[woman] There we go.

1483
01:19:08,666 --> 01:19:10,708
-The doctor will be right with you.
-Mm-hmm.

1484
01:19:18,083 --> 01:19:19,125
Mr. Peter Pan?

1485
01:19:19,708 --> 01:19:20,875
That's what it says.

1486
01:19:20,958 --> 01:19:22,708
-[laughs] Wow.
-[laughs]

1487
01:19:26,333 --> 01:19:28,041
Hello, Mr. Pan.

1488
01:19:28,125 --> 01:19:30,666
So it looks like this is
your first time with us, right?

1489
01:19:31,708 --> 01:19:34,125
What seems to be the trouble? Hm?

1490
01:19:35,291 --> 01:19:36,791
What do you want?

1491
01:19:36,875 --> 01:19:37,833
Five minutes to talk.

1492
01:19:37,916 --> 01:19:39,291
I don't care, Olli.

1493
01:19:39,375 --> 01:19:40,750
And what's with the stupid name?

1494
01:19:40,833 --> 01:19:42,833
You wouldn't've seen me otherwise.
Had to be done.

1495
01:19:42,916 --> 01:19:45,458
Well, I'm not talking to you. Now get out!

1496
01:19:45,541 --> 01:19:46,750
You're being unfair to Matze.

1497
01:19:46,833 --> 01:19:47,791
-Hey…
-[door opens]

1498
01:19:56,041 --> 01:19:58,208
Okay. We're all set. Hm?

1499
01:20:00,958 --> 01:20:02,708
-[machine whirring]
-Let's get started, Peter.

1500
01:20:02,791 --> 01:20:07,000
What? No, no. That's not necessary.
My pain just disappeared, it's a miracle.

1501
01:20:07,083 --> 01:20:09,708
Yeah, people say that a lot.
Just trust me, Mr. Pan,

1502
01:20:09,791 --> 01:20:11,916
you'll be a lot better off
if I examine you.

1503
01:20:12,000 --> 01:20:13,916
[mischievous music playing]

1504
01:20:19,916 --> 01:20:21,916
Ah… Ah!

1505
01:20:24,000 --> 01:20:24,958
Ah!

1506
01:20:28,041 --> 01:20:30,041
[Olli grunting]

1507
01:20:30,125 --> 01:20:33,041
Ah… Ah! Ah! Ah!

1508
01:20:35,083 --> 01:20:38,583
Decay on 4-8. The doctor will
give you a shot, you won't feel a thing.

1509
01:20:38,666 --> 01:20:40,708
-No, Mr. Pan's very tough.
-Huh?

1510
01:20:40,791 --> 01:20:43,750
He said he doesn't need anesthesia,
and I'm happy to oblige him.

1511
01:20:43,833 --> 01:20:45,750
[Olli] Eh? Uh, uh…

1512
01:20:45,833 --> 01:20:47,541
[air hissing]

1513
01:20:47,625 --> 01:20:49,625
[whirring]

1514
01:20:49,708 --> 01:20:51,041
Ah, ah…

1515
01:20:51,125 --> 01:20:55,916
[Olli yelling]

1516
01:20:56,000 --> 01:20:57,875
[Olli screaming]

1517
01:20:57,958 --> 01:21:00,791
Mom, I don't wanna go in there.
Please don't make me.

1518
01:21:00,875 --> 01:21:06,041
[screaming and crying]

1519
01:21:06,125 --> 01:21:08,666
[panting and whimpering]

1520
01:21:08,750 --> 01:21:10,041
[Rebecca] All righty.

1521
01:21:10,541 --> 01:21:11,791
[Olli moans]

1522
01:21:11,875 --> 01:21:12,708
Drink some water.

1523
01:21:12,791 --> 01:21:13,791
[groans]

1524
01:21:15,166 --> 01:21:18,416
[whimpering]

1525
01:21:19,208 --> 01:21:20,958
You can go, Michelle.
I'm good with this one.

1526
01:21:22,833 --> 01:21:23,833
[Olli groans]

1527
01:21:24,458 --> 01:21:25,541
[door closes]

1528
01:21:27,833 --> 01:21:29,625
So I'm being unfair here, really?

1529
01:21:29,708 --> 01:21:31,791
Matze had a bunch of opportunities
to move in with me,

1530
01:21:31,875 --> 01:21:33,250
and he fucked up every time.

1531
01:21:34,625 --> 01:21:37,625
It was my fault though.
I talked him out of it over and over.

1532
01:21:37,708 --> 01:21:40,500
Well, he wouldn't have even listened
if he was serious about us.

1533
01:21:40,583 --> 01:21:43,375
And he wouldn't have put his friend
above me and our future.

1534
01:21:44,208 --> 01:21:47,625
He's not, otherwise he would never
have kicked me out of our place!

1535
01:21:51,791 --> 01:21:53,375
-Really?
-Yeah.

1536
01:21:53,458 --> 01:21:56,041
I'm outta there.
Besides, I'm going on the world tour soon.

1537
01:21:56,125 --> 01:21:58,125
[soft music playing]

1538
01:21:59,708 --> 01:22:01,000
Give him another chance.

1539
01:22:02,000 --> 01:22:04,625
Matze misses you a lot. I mean it.

1540
01:22:11,625 --> 01:22:12,583
Olli?

1541
01:22:14,375 --> 01:22:16,958
Uh… you did have a cavity in your molar.

1542
01:22:19,083 --> 01:22:20,250
Cool.

1543
01:22:20,791 --> 01:22:22,250
[groans]

1544
01:22:22,916 --> 01:22:25,166
[man] Oh, hello. Excuse me, sir.

1545
01:22:25,250 --> 01:22:26,750
Miss Richthoff. Here. Take a look.

1546
01:22:26,833 --> 01:22:29,916
You'll be interested, I think.
Well, everyone should be interested

1547
01:22:30,000 --> 01:22:33,333
that the new
intra-oral scanner has arrived.

1548
01:22:33,416 --> 01:22:34,416
At last.

1549
01:22:36,041 --> 01:22:37,291
Miss Richthoff?

1550
01:22:41,416 --> 01:22:43,375
I'm sorry, I need time to think.

1551
01:22:45,875 --> 01:22:51,666
Miss Kaminski? Here. Look.
I believe this will be of interest to you.

1552
01:22:56,375 --> 01:22:58,708
TROUBLE WITH HAUKE. CAN WE MEET?

1553
01:23:03,750 --> 01:23:05,750
[gentle music continues]

1554
01:23:09,458 --> 01:23:10,833
[vibrates]

1555
01:23:13,000 --> 01:23:15,000
HEY MATZE, WANT TO GRAB A BITE TO EAT?

1556
01:23:34,583 --> 01:23:35,791
[sighs]

1557
01:23:39,625 --> 01:23:40,750
[sighs]

1558
01:23:47,000 --> 01:23:47,833
Hi.

1559
01:23:48,833 --> 01:23:50,041
Hey.

1560
01:23:50,125 --> 01:23:52,666
I… uh, I'm meeting Schmitti for a bite.

1561
01:23:53,416 --> 01:23:54,375
Yeah, meeting Moni.

1562
01:23:55,208 --> 01:23:56,083
Okay.

1563
01:24:15,750 --> 01:24:17,541
Have you ever eaten with Schmitti here?

1564
01:24:17,625 --> 01:24:18,833
No, it's the first time.

1565
01:24:28,625 --> 01:24:30,333
And I've never met Moni here.

1566
01:24:35,541 --> 01:24:37,333
Yeah, my guess is Olli's responsible.

1567
01:24:38,041 --> 01:24:39,291
What makes you so sure?

1568
01:24:39,375 --> 01:24:41,625
Well, he was my patient this morning.

1569
01:24:43,333 --> 01:24:45,166
He told me you finally kicked him out.

1570
01:24:45,250 --> 01:24:47,250
He didn't grill you about it
or anything, did he?

1571
01:24:47,333 --> 01:24:49,416
Not at all. It was the reverse, he…

1572
01:24:50,500 --> 01:24:51,833
took your side, actually.

1573
01:24:52,416 --> 01:24:53,458
He was committed.

1574
01:24:53,541 --> 01:24:57,416
So much so that he… got
some serious treatment without anesthesia.

1575
01:24:58,666 --> 01:25:00,416
We talking about the same Olli?

1576
01:25:00,500 --> 01:25:02,500
[soft music playing]

1577
01:25:03,958 --> 01:25:06,458
Somehow he managed
to arrange this meeting.

1578
01:25:06,541 --> 01:25:08,708
[waiter] Afternoon, guys.
What can I get you?

1579
01:25:09,666 --> 01:25:12,083
I think we maybe need a moment.

1580
01:25:12,166 --> 01:25:13,250
No problem.

1581
01:25:17,791 --> 01:25:18,750
Maybe we should decide.

1582
01:25:32,791 --> 01:25:34,958
So now you're living there
all by yourself?

1583
01:25:36,458 --> 01:25:37,291
Yep.

1584
01:25:38,666 --> 01:25:39,666
And you?

1585
01:25:40,583 --> 01:25:42,166
Still hoping for a new place?

1586
01:25:47,625 --> 01:25:49,500
I have one in mind.

1587
01:25:49,583 --> 01:25:51,458
There's a whole lot of room for you.

1588
01:25:52,791 --> 01:25:56,125
Although the kitchen has
severe fire damage somehow.

1589
01:25:59,416 --> 01:26:01,875
I wanna cover all the repairs, okay?

1590
01:26:05,041 --> 01:26:06,333
No way.

1591
01:26:06,416 --> 01:26:08,875
Look, please, just… please.

1592
01:26:08,958 --> 01:26:10,375
It would make me feel better.

1593
01:26:10,958 --> 01:26:12,458
What do you mean?

1594
01:26:14,875 --> 01:26:16,333
It's a long story.

1595
01:26:16,416 --> 01:26:18,708
I promise I'll tell you later.

1596
01:26:18,791 --> 01:26:21,208
I'm just so happy
we have each other again.

1597
01:26:22,166 --> 01:26:24,958
[emotional music playing]

1598
01:26:41,666 --> 01:26:42,666
-Morning.
-[man] Hello.

1599
01:26:42,750 --> 01:26:43,791
[woman] Hi, Matze.

1600
01:27:00,458 --> 01:27:03,000
I SOLD YOUR TICKET. OLLI

1601
01:27:06,125 --> 01:27:07,208
Where's Olli's stuff?

1602
01:27:08,208 --> 01:27:09,875
Hello to you, Matze.

1603
01:27:11,166 --> 01:27:12,458
Why ask me about it?

1604
01:27:13,083 --> 01:27:16,625
Oh no.
Did Batman and Robin go to splitsville?

1605
01:27:17,916 --> 01:27:22,125
Listen, your friend quit so he could
go on his round the world vision quest.

1606
01:27:22,208 --> 01:27:24,541
But it seems like
you came to your senses, right?

1607
01:27:24,625 --> 01:27:25,750
I don't blame you.

1608
01:27:25,833 --> 01:27:27,750
That kinda trip wouldn't be for me either.

1609
01:27:27,833 --> 01:27:31,000
Living out of a backpack,
staying in cheap hostels,

1610
01:27:31,083 --> 01:27:32,583
never showering… Ugh!

1611
01:27:35,541 --> 01:27:39,583
Uh, oh… so Holloscheck from
our luxury properties division is leaving.

1612
01:27:39,666 --> 01:27:41,458
That'd be a good position for you.

1613
01:27:41,541 --> 01:27:47,125
Larger commissions, better salary,
but a lot of hard work too.

1614
01:27:47,833 --> 01:27:48,875
You can think about it.

1615
01:27:48,958 --> 01:27:49,958
I'm good, actually.

1616
01:27:51,041 --> 01:27:53,375
I accept the offer. Thank you.

1617
01:27:55,208 --> 01:27:57,041
Uh… you have any idea
when Olli's flying out?

1618
01:27:57,125 --> 01:27:59,250
Um… I think this morning?

1619
01:27:59,333 --> 01:28:01,333
["Lucky Man" by The Verve playing]

1620
01:28:12,375 --> 01:28:14,500
<i>Hey, it's Olli. Sorry,</i>
<i>I'm just trying to find my phone.</i>

1621
01:28:14,583 --> 01:28:15,666
Shit.

1622
01:28:38,250 --> 01:28:41,125
<i>♪ Happiness, more or less ♪</i>

1623
01:28:41,208 --> 01:28:44,291
<i>♪ It's just a change in me</i>
<i>Something in my liberty ♪</i>

1624
01:28:44,958 --> 01:28:48,875
<i>♪ Oh, my, my ♪</i>

1625
01:28:50,875 --> 01:28:53,791
<i>♪ Happiness, coming and going… ♪</i>

1626
01:28:54,458 --> 01:28:57,541
-Sorry, could you do me a favor, please?
-First of all, you need to get in line.

1627
01:28:57,625 --> 01:29:00,291
Uh, uh… I… I-I'm trying to find s-s--

1628
01:29:00,375 --> 01:29:01,916
Hey! No cutting in line!

1629
01:29:02,750 --> 01:29:03,750
Olli!

1630
01:29:05,458 --> 01:29:06,291
Hey.

1631
01:29:06,375 --> 01:29:08,708
What, did you change your mind?
No ticket for you, sorry.

1632
01:29:08,791 --> 01:29:10,708
Becky told me
you went to make things right.

1633
01:29:10,791 --> 01:29:12,541
Oh, so my matchmaking was a success?

1634
01:29:12,625 --> 01:29:13,875
It all worked out, we're good.

1635
01:29:14,791 --> 01:29:18,083
Is that true… for us too? I hope it is.

1636
01:29:18,708 --> 01:29:20,250
Thanks for being a great friend.

1637
01:29:21,583 --> 01:29:25,750
[woman over PA] <i>Final boarding call</i>
<i>for flight TH8431 with service to Bangkok.</i>

1638
01:29:25,833 --> 01:29:27,375
So, this is it. It's happening.

1639
01:29:27,458 --> 01:29:28,916
<i>Passengers please proceed…</i>

1640
01:29:29,000 --> 01:29:31,750
Yeah. Guess I better
camp under the Northern Lights.

1641
01:29:31,833 --> 01:29:33,791
Otherwise, all that cold training
will go to waste.

1642
01:29:33,875 --> 01:29:35,458
[laughing]

1643
01:29:35,541 --> 01:29:36,416
[Pia whistles sharply]

1644
01:29:38,041 --> 01:29:39,166
Who's that?

1645
01:29:39,250 --> 01:29:42,458
Um, Pia. She took your ticket, man.

1646
01:29:42,541 --> 01:29:45,000
My buddy Matze! All is forgiven!

1647
01:29:45,583 --> 01:29:47,041
Amazing! Come on!

1648
01:29:48,625 --> 01:29:50,750
-Yeah, I should…
-All right, then.

1649
01:29:53,625 --> 01:29:56,750
<i>♪ How many corners do I have to turn? ♪</i>

1650
01:29:57,750 --> 01:30:00,166
It's crazy. I think the longest
we've been away from each other

1651
01:30:00,250 --> 01:30:02,916
was in elementary school
when we'd get three days for Christmas.

1652
01:30:04,250 --> 01:30:06,916
That's true. The year will fly by though.

1653
01:30:07,000 --> 01:30:08,541
Yeah, you're right.

1654
01:30:08,625 --> 01:30:11,083
Yeah but, uh,
a year can feel like an eternity too.

1655
01:30:11,166 --> 01:30:12,458
Yeah, that's true.

1656
01:30:13,583 --> 01:30:14,666
[Pia whistles]

1657
01:30:19,583 --> 01:30:20,416
Okay, take care.

1658
01:30:21,375 --> 01:30:22,416
You too.

1659
01:30:22,500 --> 01:30:24,500
[song continues]

1660
01:30:31,916 --> 01:30:34,625
<i>♪ Happiness, more or less ♪</i>

1661
01:30:34,708 --> 01:30:38,166
<i>♪ Is just a change in me</i>
<i>Something in my liberty ♪</i>

1662
01:30:38,250 --> 01:30:40,916
<i>♪ Happiness, coming and going ♪</i>

1663
01:30:41,000 --> 01:30:44,750
<i>♪ I watch you look at me</i>
<i>Watch my fever growing on ♪</i>

1664
01:30:44,833 --> 01:30:49,625
<i>♪ Oh, my, my ♪</i>

1665
01:30:51,208 --> 01:30:55,625
<i>♪ Oh, my, my ♪</i>

1666
01:30:57,583 --> 01:31:02,333
<i>♪ Oh, my, my ♪</i>

1667
01:31:10,666 --> 01:31:11,875
[song ends]

1668
01:31:16,958 --> 01:31:18,125
<i>Eyyy!</i>

1669
01:31:18,208 --> 01:31:19,750
<i>Oh, stop.</i>

1670
01:31:19,833 --> 01:31:21,375
What happened, you two?

1671
01:31:21,458 --> 01:31:23,583
<i>I mean, well, I proposed and she said yes.</i>

1672
01:31:23,666 --> 01:31:25,583
Okay, right what happened exactly?

1673
01:31:25,666 --> 01:31:28,541
'Cause, Olli, I know getting married
wasn't on the top of your list, right?

1674
01:31:28,625 --> 01:31:31,041
<i>Well, we were hanging out</i>
<i>by this super cold lake in Iceland,</i>

1675
01:31:31,125 --> 01:31:33,000
<i>with incredible views</i>
<i>of the Northern Lights,</i>

1676
01:31:33,083 --> 01:31:35,458
<i>and we're standing in a long line</i>
<i>to rent some wetsuits,</i>

1677
01:31:35,541 --> 01:31:38,333
<i>and I look over and suddenly Pia says,</i>
<i>"Screw wetsuits!"</i>

1678
01:31:38,416 --> 01:31:40,500
<i>And jumps into the lake</i>
<i>without batting an eye.</i>

1679
01:31:40,583 --> 01:31:43,333
<i>I mean, obviously</i>
<i>I had to marry that woman, right?</i>

1680
01:31:43,416 --> 01:31:44,250
[all laughing]

1681
01:31:44,333 --> 01:31:46,583
<i>I only married him to shield you guys</i>
<i>from further torture.</i>

1682
01:31:46,666 --> 01:31:49,250
Oh. Thanks a lot. That's sweet.

1683
01:31:49,333 --> 01:31:52,166
And, um, yeah, congratulations,
Olli's not an easy adversary.

1684
01:31:53,416 --> 01:31:54,375
God!

1685
01:31:59,000 --> 01:32:01,458
<i>Oh, one more thing. Bali is amazing.</i>

1686
01:32:01,541 --> 01:32:03,625
<i>-Take some time off and come out here!</i>
<i>-Yeah.</i>

1687
01:32:03,708 --> 01:32:05,250
<i>Matze, Becky.</i>

1688
01:32:06,458 --> 01:32:07,458
<i>-Ciao!</i>
<i>-Cheers.</i>

1689
01:32:07,541 --> 01:32:08,833
Ciao.

1690
01:32:09,750 --> 01:32:11,208
Oh, sweet.

1691
01:32:11,291 --> 01:32:12,625
[doorbell rings]

1692
01:32:22,875 --> 01:32:24,083
[man] Hey, Matze.

1693
01:32:25,208 --> 01:32:26,791
It's… It's Schmitti.

1694
01:32:27,583 --> 01:32:29,083
Antje found his secret weed stash

1695
